ed on``train_sizes``.\n1458 | \n1459 |     random_state : int, RandomState instance or None, default=None\n1460 |         Used when ``shuffle`` is True. Pass an int for reproducible\n1461 |         output across multiple function calls.\n1462 |         See :term:`Glossary <random_state>`.\n1463 | \n1464 |     error_score : 'raise' or numeric, default=np.nan\n1465 |         Value to assign to the score if an error occurs in estimator fitting.\n1466 |         If set to 'raise', the error is raised.\n1467 |         If a numeric value is given, FitFailedWarning is raised.\n1468 | \n1469 |         .. versionadded:: 0.20\n1470 | \n1471 |     return_times : bool, default=False\n1472 |         Whether to return the fit and score times.\n1473 | \n1474 |     fit_params : dict, default=None\n1475 |         Parameters to pass to the fit method of the estimator.\n1476 | \n1477 |         .. versionadded:: 0.24\n1478 | \n1479 |     Returns\n1480 |     -------\n1481 |     train_sizes_abs : array of shape (n_unique_ticks,)\n1482 |         Numbers of training examples that has been used to generate the\n1483 |         learning curve. Note that the number of ticks might be less\n1484 |         than n_ticks because duplicate entries will be removed.\n1485 | \n1486 |     train_scores : array of shape (n_ticks, n_cv_folds)\n1487 |         Scores on training sets.\n1488 | \n1489 |     test_scores : array of shape (n_ticks, n_cv_folds)\n1490 |         Scores on test set.\n1491 | \n1492 |     fit_times : array of shape (n_ticks, n_cv_folds)\n1493 |         Times spent for fitting in seconds. Only present if ``return_times``\n1494 |         is True.\n1495 | \n1496 |     score_times : array of shape (n_ticks, n_cv_folds)\n1497 |         Times spent for scoring in seconds. Only present if ``return_times``\n1498 |         is True.\n1499 | \n1500 |     Notes\n1501 |     -----\n1502 |     See :ref:`examples/model_selection/plot_learning_curve.py\n1503 |     <sphx_glr_auto_examples_model_selection