ort Hidden, Interval, StrOptions\n  28 | from ..model_selection import check_cv\n  29 | from ..exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n  30 | from ..utils.parallel import delayed, Parallel\n  31 | \n  32 | SOLVE_TRIANGULAR_ARGS = {\"check_finite\": False}\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/_build_utils/__init__.py:gen_from_templates`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 87 | def gen_from_templates(templates):\n 88 |     \"\"\"Generate cython files from a list of templates\"\"\"\n 89 |     # Lazy import because cython is not a runtime dependency.\n 90 |     from Cython import Tempita\n 91 | \n 92 |     for template in templates:\n 93 |         outfile = template.replace(\".tp\", \"\")\n 94 | \n 95 |         # if the template is not updated, no need to output the cython file\n 96 |         if not (\n 97 |             os.path.exists(outfile)\n 98 |             and os.stat(template).st_mtime < os.stat(outfile).st_mtime\n 99 |         ):\n100 |             with open(template, \"r\") as f:\n101 |                 tmpl = f.read()\n102 | \n103 |             tmpl_ = Tempita.sub(tmpl)\n104 | \n105 |             warn_msg = (\n106 |                 \"# WARNING: Do not edit this file directly.\\n\"\n107 |                 f\"# It is automatically generated from {template!r}.\\n\"\n108 |                 \"# Changes must be made there.\\n\\n\"\n109 |             )\n110 | \n111 |             with open(outfile, \"w\") as f:\n112 |                 f.write(warn_msg)\n113 |                 f.write(tmpl_)\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py:SplineTransformer._get_base_knot_positions`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n722 | def _get_base_knot_positions(X, n_knots=10, knots=\"uniform\", sample_weight=None):\n723 |         \"\"\"Calculate base knot positions.\n724 | \n725 |         Base knots such that first knot <= feature <= last knot. For the\n726 |         B-spline construction with scipy.interpolate.BSpline, 2*degree knots\n727 |         beyond the base interval are added.\n728 | \n729 |         Returns\n730 |         -------\n731 |         knots : ndarray of shape (n_knots, n_features), dtype=np.float64\n732 |             Knot positions (points) of base interval.\n733 |         \"\"\"\n734 |         if knots == \"quantile\":\n735 |             percentiles = 100 * np.linspace(\n736 |                 start=0, stop=1, num=n_knots, dtype=np.float64\n737 |             )\n738 | \n739 |             if sample_weight is None:\n740 |                 knots = np.percentile(X, percentiles, axis=0)\n741 |             else:\n742 |                 knots = np.array(\n743 |                     [\n744 |                         _weighted_percentile(X, sample_weight, percentile)\n745 |                         for percentile in percentiles\n746 |                     ]\n747 |                 )\n748 | \n749 |         else:\n750 |             # knots == 'uniform':\n751 |             # Note that the variable `knots` has already been validated and\n752 |             # `else` is therefore safe.\n753 |             # Disregard observations with zero weight.\n754 |             mask = slice(None, None, 1) if sample_weight is None else sample_weight > 0\n755 |             x_min = np.amin(X[mask], axis=0)\n756 |             x_max = np.amax(X[mask], axis=0)\n757 | \n758 |             knots = np.linspace(\n759 |                 start=x_min,\n760 |                 stop=x_max,\n761 |                 num=n_knots,\n762 |                 endpoint=True,\n763 |                 dtype=np.float64,\n764 |             )\n765 | \n766 |         return knots\n```\n\nFound file `examples/ensemble/plot_forest_importances.py`.\nFound file `examples/mixture/plot_gmm_init.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, here are the key locations that need modification to implement sparse matrix output for SplineTransformer:\n\n```\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py\nline: 10\nline: 11\nline: 106\nline: 914-921\nline: 943-950\nclass: SplineTransformer\nfunction: transform\nfunction: __init__\n\nsklearn/utils/validation.py\nline: 1\nfunction: check_array\n\nsklearn/utils/_param_validation.py\nline: 1\nfunction: Interval\nfunction: StrOptions\n\nsklearn/utils/stats.py\nline: 1\nfunction: _weighted_percentile\n\nsklearn/preprocessing/_csr_polynomial_expansion.py\nline: 1\nline: 2\nline: 3\nline: 4\nline: 5\nfunction: _csr_polynomial_expansion\nfunction: _calc_expanded_nnz\nfunction: _calc_total_nnz\n```\n\nThe main changes needed are:\n\n1. The primary SplineTransformer class in sklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py needs modifications:\n   - Need to add a new parameter `sparse` to __init__ and save it as an instance variable\n   - In the transform method, check if sparse mode is enabled and use scipy's sparse matrix functionality instead of dense arrays\n   - The current implementation uses dense arrays throughout the transformation (lines 914-921 in transform() method)\n   - Lines 943-950 (inside transform()) create large dense matrices that would need to be converted to sparse format\n\n2. The validation utilities in sklearn/utils/validation.py and _param_validation.py will need updates to validate the new sparse parameter\n\n3. The csr_polynomial_expansion utilities in _csr_polynomial_expansion.py would need to be updated to work with sparse matrices\n\n4. The stats utility (_stats.py) would need modifications to work with sparse versions of calculated statistics\n\nThese changes would allow the SplineTransformer to return sparse matrix output when initialized with sparse=True, taking advantage of scipy's new sparse design matrix functionality introduced in PR #1444.\n\nThe core modification points are:\n- Adding sparse parameter support in SplineTransformer.__init__\n- Using scipy's design_matrix from PR #1434\n- Modifying the matrix creation in transform() to handle sparse cases\n- Updating dependent utility functions to work with sparse matrices when enabled\n\nThis localization focuses on the key files and functions that need to be modified to implement the sparse matrix output feature while maintaining the existing functionality when sparse=False.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` or `get_trace_data_dependencies` again with more precise filters before finishing.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the findings by checking additional dependencies and references.\n\nFirst, let's check for any dependencies of SplineTransformer:\n\n<function=explore_tree_structure>\n<parameter=start_entities>['sklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py:SplineTransformer']</parameter>\n<parameter=direction>both</parameter>\n<parameter=dependency_type_filter>['imports', 'invokes']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "explore_tree_structure", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py:SplineTransformer\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 imports-by \u2500\u2500 sklearn/preprocessing/_