width*. The vertical baseline\n2333 |         is *bottom* (default 0).\n2334 | \n2335 |         Many parameters can take either a single value applying to all bars\n2336 |         or a sequence of values, one for each bar.\n2337 | \n2338 |         Parameters\n2339 |         ----------\n2340 |         x : float or array-like\n2341 |             The x coordinates of the bars. See also *align* for the\n2342 |             alignment of the bars to the coordinates.\n2343 | \n2344 |         height : float or array-like\n2345 |             The height(s) of the bars.\n2346 | \n2347 |             Note that if *bottom* has units (e.g. datetime), *height* should be in\n2348 |             units that are a difference from the value of *bottom* (e.g. timedelta).\n2349 | \n2350 |         width : float or array-like, default: 0.8\n2351 |             The width(s) of the bars.\n2352 | \n2353 |             Note that if *x* has units (e.g. datetime), then *width* should be in\n2354 |             units that are a difference (e.g. timedelta) around the *x* values.\n2355 | \n2356 |         bottom : float or array-like, default: 0\n2357 |             The y coordinate(s) of the bottom side(s) of the bars.\n2358 | \n2359 |             Note that if *bottom* has units, then the y-axis will get a Locator and\n2360 |             Formatter appropriate for the units (e.g. dates, or categorical).\n2361 | \n2362 |         align : {'center', 'edge'}, default: 'center'\n2363 |             Alignment of the bars to the *x* coordinates:\n2364 | \n2365 |             - 'center': Center the base on the *x* positions.\n2366 |             - 'edge': Align the left edges of the bars with the *x* positions.\n2367 | \n2368 |             To align the bars on the right edge pass a negative *width* and\n2369 |             ``align='edge'``.\n2370 | \n2371 |         Returns\n2372 |         -------\n2373 |         `.BarContainer`\n2374 |             Container with all the bars and optionally errorbars.\n2375 | \n2376 | 